    <node id="Management">
      <data key="d0">Management</data>
      <data key="d1">Concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Management is an activity that incurs organizational costs and is often used in companies as an organizing form. It involves finding and connecting people and resources to tasks, projects, and targets. Management encompasses planning, motivating, coordinating, and controlling employees, and is a crucial aspect of organizational design, ensuring tasks are completed effectively. It involves balancing cooperation and competition, and can refer to the act of managing or the people in charge of an organization.

Management includes planning, distributing resources, checking, registering, motivating, and developing. It is the act or manner of controlling and directing a company or other entity, and the skillful handling of resources. Management can be divided into social and technical scripts and is a practice of managing and organizing, particularly in problem-solving and social issues. It involves organizing and coordinating resources to achieve specific goals, and is a key element in the development and deployment of new management concepts.

Management is the practice of overseeing and controlling a business or organization, or a specific aspect of it, and directing activities within an organization. It is a process of addressing problems and implementing solutions, often requiring a long-term perspective and structural approaches. Management is also the process of dealing with or controlling things or people, and organizing and controlling resources to achieve organizational goals.

Management is the process of planning, organizing, and controlling resources to achieve specific goals. It includes planning, organizing, leading, and controlling resources to achieve organizational goals. The text discusses the need to reinvent management, including fundamental innovation in management practices and the implementation of blockchain. Management also refers to the process of running and controlling an organization. The impact of management on the financial sector is also discussed.
</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1718ba4bf71919b628b4a5d18d5dfb92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8de7684eaa9214e3bd145ee0ad6dd5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f15a70031415a373cab08355dc72cc16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb325ff3876e609f14b5256360d8deec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80bcfc5e0491a38a57bdcf5b7453e3c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35d3d3b65e002a54a8e09b9f90632d33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4198bb76b5c7a4e6c4e4bf6a530fdec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e159991e1f1aeb8a0169a48ad5b8333&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28f47105685e32bdc3711b0bd362402d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b1b2e6998da7248b40cca99640c4fc8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4584c12e3206f6c6114919230c973aa0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5ddf3937d82ce7155cb82041f93c070&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9bb1f5dfc6645013b98c9aa9eb80594&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bdc886b23f3ebaa015732c5dc3db208&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-daf93ecb6c683f40f1d34d737bcdd9fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f17aa88b9f9fb9cfeb11aa13c729db3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41a843f58092dcd2d74d07ae3cbb50cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd9bd6f99a4d3a44dfd7145bcf2becde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bf9689960b5a615f73160647f45eb4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5372fca27605b863c92a206f40e7d1ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b02c2f74cf5311b123fc2d1fdc7af1da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c205a06d6f77d9602ba2b4ac60c1b9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87e713bd8bb06b630d3292777d69ba82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25021390b7769b80eb6565268f6a339e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e554ae841a9d31896009d6df8e3254e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0652a3175020e032bf00efd7d7470b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5fa8321e4431dc130b5cfcafedecff7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea9da2d129b1ea0eedd60a5debc5dab2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39148928fd5d1cbfefc9985e1fbb32e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e434c5dc41753c53be5ce36200fdf6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c4ce5447e396cdd3bf137858b73ad36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee92635ddcf90a64b087c72dedf9473d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d98a59ed81543294260a33227b3460f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a18658aae4eca132d93e07ad23124b02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f0573de7c7cbde2e2975eead953b1b1</data>
