    <node id="Transactions">
      <data key="d0">Transactions</data>
      <data key="d1">Concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Transactions are actions recorded on a blockchain, representing the exchange of value or information. They encompass various steps and are executed via a protocol. Transactions can be instances of buying or selling something, acting as a business deal, or the exchange of goods or services. Within the Bitcoin network, transactions are financial exchanges, specifically the exchange of Bitcoin, verified by nodes and arranged in chronological order.
</data>
