    </node>
    <node id="Automattic">
      <data key="d0">Automattic</data>
      <data key="d1">Organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A distributed company.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e4198bb76b5c7a4e6c4e4bf6a530fdec</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Organization">
      <data key="d0">Organization</data>
      <data key="d1">Organization</data>
      <data key="d2">An **organization** is fundamentally a group of people working together, often structured, for a common purpose or to achieve a common goal. This can encompass various forms, including businesses, societies, associations, and cooperatives. Organizations are formed with a particular purpose in mind and may be involved in solving problems. They can range from traditional entities with permanent employees, structures, and internal systems to newer models like Weconomics. The structure and arrangement of individuals and resources within an organization are crucial for achieving its specific goals. The concept of an organization is also relevant in the context of blockchain technology, with discussions on how it impacts organizational structures and models, and how organizations may consider or implement blockchain. An organization can be created through mergers of institutions, resulting in a building, employees, an organogram, a structure, a culture, and its own ICT system.
</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1718ba4bf71919b628b4a5d18d5dfb92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3be89e365c019f2fcc2432c91f0e473b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9fc0782a2ca0ad992c87fd04cc684c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f77d5a4ad60f6ba2fd71299d648a478&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-760373765c10662d9065ee92ab95d40e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4198bb76b5c7a4e6c4e4bf6a530fdec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-450d7f7ac5a7955ebd244cd286eca610&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bb7630f85643e1cb2d411ec7e989e2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8c6bc06eea895d8032b78c8f25780c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50f3afddce8bc964731907b7d70c528d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc15fe668555752ca731b2fc192c1d71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a077a85d3f0dd5b451d9b582ad0180e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a15e0f6d912773be3b201f8652ca407&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41a843f58092dcd2d74d07ae3cbb50cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ef570382baecc1b0372c031d77bc626&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5372fca27605b863c92a206f40e7d1ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d58bb4eb1c8acda232b201e69b419a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92a25fd0e21cd743e62c34c35ca67a06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ff3172a1b829e75497860c94f161e61&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11b8cc34d6b3608e77a895b028c9a6d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1900d9fbbbeb4ce6f5731ed0181e0729&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffabef43b19d5a643510bc7775c449e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7b4cfcb5217fb678295a92b2dce1add&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e7516ac1d2c2eabb8e7a0eb0c8233aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5764b11860bd97da66e34d549f66280&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5fa8321e4431dc130b5cfcafedecff7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f03d2d17c7bf1cc4e87ff716b4c883a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03ab58813161f8d97d9bd6f12223a7b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-158f8bc907835844a3f304c334f72115&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f0573de7c7cbde2e2975eead953b1b1</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Span of Control">
      <data key="d0">Span of Control</data>
      <data key="d1">Concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The number of subordinates a manager can effectively supervise.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e4198bb76b5c7a4e6c4e4bf6a530fdec</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Money">
      <data key="d0">Money</data>
      <data key="d1">Concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Money is a current medium of exchange, typically in the form of coins and banknotes, and is collectively referred to as currency. It functions as a medium of exchange, a unit of account, and a store of value, facilitating the exchange of values.
</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fb778237d5f161db3ea1b80dc6c348cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d416cde8eabae677d0912ce737cda600&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d9c783fe7141c81f49edd0fdc5f7e7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ff3172a1b829e75497860c94f161e61&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0158f505b78daad05d6ccc48a0249c4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e434c5dc41753c53be5ce36200fdf6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25021390b7769b80eb6565268f6a339e</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Contracts">
      <data key="d0">Contracts</data>
      <data key="d1">Concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A traditional institution used to reduce trust.&lt;SEP&gt;A written or spoken agreement, especially one concerning employment, sales, or tenancy, that is intended to be enforceable by law.&lt;SEP&gt;Agreements used in bilateral trading and cooperation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-25021390b7769b80eb6565268f6a339e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4584c12e3206f6c6114919230c973aa0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e434c5dc41753c53be5ce36200fdf6b</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Brands">
      <data key="d0">Brands</data>
      <data key="d1">Concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A type of product manufactured by a particular company under a particular name.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-25021390b7769b80eb6565268f6a339e</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Laws">
      <data key="d0">Laws</data>
      <data key="d1">Policy</data>
      <data key="d2">Legal regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;The system of rules that a particular country or community recognizes as regulating the actions of its members and may enforce by the imposition of penalties.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-25021390b7769b80eb6565268f6a339e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21cef8e27910469220297abed08fe4b9</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Companies">
      <data key="d0">Companies</data>
      <data key="d1">Organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Companies are a type of business entity, representing an association of people with a shared purpose. They are commercial entities that sell goods or services to make a profit, and are often involved in both cooperation and competition. These organizations utilize management and hierarchy, and interact with the government and citizens. Many existing companies are part of the current social-economic establishment and need to adapt their strategy and structure. They are often seen as building applications on top of the blockchain infrastructure, rather than developing the infrastructure itself. Within companies, the use of Blockchain Organizing may be limited, and learned helplessness can manifest during change processes.
</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-23db6b509ce85251954b0c6eceb7e526&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0197eeb8e7c7c337867cce9066008c24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0fba0b4043ec1b0d668ebbd78ac72b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3601da3b0bece1d5e1adfbd71567fa8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d95f9e583e2983dc31135025ee88cc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4dff72475ff38066f492d4c69fb7ef24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c4e508645dafe5462c20f99b327c186&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc2e798f6204ea8604bf022cbeb2db21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4584c12e3206f6c6114919230c973aa0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f03d2d17c7bf1cc4e87ff716b4c883a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e434c5dc41753c53be5ce36200fdf6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33012de7a0074f352d461a49b8eb5bc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd3a806efebda5a1804e8f5fe8891b19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25021390b7769b80eb6565268f6a339e</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Banks">
      <data key="d0">Banks</data>
      <data key="d1">Organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A financial institution licensed to receive deposits and make loans.&lt;SEP&gt;Entities mentioned as controlling the social-economic system.&lt;SEP&gt;Financial institutions involved in the existing social-economic establishment.&lt;SEP&gt;Financial institutions that hold and manage money.&lt;SEP&gt;Financial institutions that provide services such as accepting deposits, making loans, and providing financial products.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cf141e4f6e7a26acb29505682821d79c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0158f505b78daad05d6ccc48a0249c4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c4e508645dafe5462c20f99b327c186&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25021390b7769b80eb6565268f6a339e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0697bcc736e38c4eecf7ba0b89208980</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Governments">
      <data key="d0">Governments</data>
      <data key="d1">Organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Governments are the governing bodies of a state, nation, or community, and are also the system by which a state or community is governed. They are involved in the existing social-economic establishment and play a role in promoting innovation. Governments often outsource services and participate in the network community. They are also organizations involved in the development of technical innovations.
</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b1d935bc8938352c154222fd6602c580&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c4e508645dafe5462c20f99b327c186&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f03d2d17c7bf1cc4e87ff716b4c883a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33012de7a0074f352d461a49b8eb5bc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd3a806efebda5a1804e8f5fe8891b19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25021390b7769b80eb6565268f6a339e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b863d6e3078036af759c206058182dc</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Economy">
      <data key="d0">Economy</data>
      <data key="d1">Concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The **economy** is a multifaceted concept encompassing the system of trade, industry, and the production, distribution, and consumption of goods and services. It represents the wealth and resources of a country or region, particularly concerning the production and consumption of goods and services. Furthermore, the economy is related to Blockchain Organizing.
</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2ebde21af6f93489c1d70ecb9ced229b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f4323a294fdbd03686f0af42313fca3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3f00be44fc7922f83a9376fe1a72137&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc20e87e2ee483ddd4598fa7842b42be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5764b11860bd97da66e34d549f66280&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0158f505b78daad05d6ccc48a0249c4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-691633ed3dd644b2a539f78fc15edeca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25021390b7769b80eb6565268f6a339e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-248aad6ba79eb8e5e5f575bda42587cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce508aba4aa5d17fb6f6c48acdcd7ca8</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Society">
      <data key="d0">Society</data>
      <data key="d1">Concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A group of people living together in an organized community.&lt;SEP&gt;The aggregate of people living together in a more or less ordered community.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-46057989310d5a9fbbe08e681d5994eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25021390b7769b80eb6565268f6a339e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f77553720c7b4f6a28c759fc456fbcd9</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Agents">
      <data key="d0">Agents</data>
      <data key="d1">Concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A person or thing that takes an active role or produces a specified effect.&lt;SEP&gt;Entities or individuals involved in processes, whose role is reduced or eliminated by blockchain technology.&lt;SEP&gt;Tools used to reduce insecurity and organize trust. Also referred to as institutions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4322631c6ab79cfbe8d80ecc2f1dee23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25021390b7769b80eb6565268f6a339e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d58bb4eb1c8acda232b201e69b419a6</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Institutions">
      <data key="d0">Institutions</data>
      <data key="d1">Concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Institutions are societies or organizations established for various purposes, including religious, educational, and social objectives. They function as tools for executing market transactions and are a form of organized capacity. Institutions play a role in reducing insecurity and organizing trust, often referred to as agents. They are also involved in transactions that are reduced or eliminated through the use of smart contracts. Furthermore, they are organizations that organize trust, and are involved in reducing insecurity.
</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4f17aa88b9f9fb9cfeb11aa13c729db3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d58bb4eb1c8acda232b201e69b419a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1159f0e0de86630155e1bc94285ff20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76a98cc533bce6a2d78638ddd7af06e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25021390b7769b80eb6565268f6a339e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c32e29b3b9db8610104f31940dd08f8</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Bitcoin">
      <data key="d0">Bitcoin</data>
      <data key="d1">Technology</data>
      <data key="d2">Bitcoin is a cryptocurrency and a decentralized digital payment system. It is the first and most well-known cryptocurrency, released by Nakamoto. Bitcoin is a specific application and implementation of blockchain technology, serving as proof of concept for its long-term viability, stability, and utility. It is a blockchain application for digital money, facilitating value transfer from seller to buyer. Transactions are recorded in a decentralized accounting system and distributed across participating nodes. Bitcoin is also the name of the cryptocurrency itself, often referred to as BTC. It is a digital or virtual currency that uses cryptography for security and operates on a blockchain, a distributed public ledger. It is a peer-to-peer electronic cash system and a medium of exchange supported by a protocol and a community. Its value is based on trust and belief in its future value. Bitcoin can take many forms and is often contrasted with blockchain technology. It is a form of digital money or value that includes software code or programmable money. A total of 21 million Bitcoins can be made, and each can be divided into 100,000,000 units (Satoshi's) up to 8 decimal places. It is a cryptocurrency that can be used for payment and is mentioned in the context of wallet software and financial articles. It is a cryptocurrency and the system it operates on. It is a blockchain community where values are created and exchanged.
</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2d666492c06b72b3acdaaf417a46ebbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d9c783fe7141c81f49edd0fdc5f7e7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14ccd99dba07cc2c31752c9fb5125f23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6356289eb89ea3c9fb9f8aeb2f5cfa59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae10fd627995a83f8cbe34b2cc884afb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c4e508645dafe5462c20f99b327c186&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dcb530cf287b37d28b085c805c61d13c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35554d8f41f52c69d22444b00c08876e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35d3d3b65e002a54a8e09b9f90632d33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a62990abf7c11921583ee875b388e787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-efb1e3dfd567d51e6d05f0dc833e60f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29858535f8646a6325b1db80639f647f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb778237d5f161db3ea1b80dc6c348cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54ae90ff07e4d84d7a1591868bfd384c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19098cf3a0c49ab4c21a0a5dd8820f48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd3a806efebda5a1804e8f5fe8891b19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0697bcc736e38c4eecf7ba0b89208980&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7aaa6822f8a76a5ed5c426555be8b15f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ef570382baecc1b0372c031d77bc626&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d8c581b75ce0f3a97084b5afbc810e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3616e23745945cf7521047d73b382ad9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f90a9e3d42822d671bf599944b3ba7ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ff3172a1b829e75497860c94f161e61&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11304546e84047544f7ab77d780c1f76&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97bf1ff7a9a0ca25ab9f8d5aef1c0355&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ba7d2662c30d83dd2e16a7c0cb197ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51acb320616574b3b600a83911d634cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c450f48104718c81f1f7df7492138e83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66c04437d924c888b68f0a652726f850&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0dd82da1fab20609f22f1ba5505c2c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c97cbc55e4d5c208212c7c5fab62f82e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04f3d062a707dfb7235caa4e344995d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f95a0611fe1d32637a403d767d70c8bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62af45e2578182bc4b36cffed9534e81</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Management Model">
      <data key="d0">Management Model</data>
      <data key="d1">Concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The **Management Model** is a framework or approach used to manage and organize activities, resources, and people within an organization. It is a model for managing a system, and is particularly relevant in the context of Blockchain Organizing. This model emphasizes efficiency and minimizing friction, and is crucial for the successful implementation of blockchain technology. It also involves a willingness to change existing institutions. The Management Model can be viewed as a new approach to managing work, and is also mentioned in the context of innovation.
</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-dcbc07b460eacb096f4663b63a5541e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97bf1ff7a9a0ca25ab9f8d5aef1c0355&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7a4f0543c997bbae168f719fdd65986&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af499d61f5968bcd65d0631a51264c34&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c7ba153eb5a0d7f103744153505eb9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45e51e7c90e9ae8cae4de232532d5451&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5f5768652d04cf68f3ca04301ae0b84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f03d2d17c7bf1cc4e87ff716b4c883a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdf7f03bab56e9193f4290651ca3c42c</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Producer">
      <data key="d0">Producer</data>
      <data key="d1">Stakeholder</data>
      <data key="d2">An entity that creates or supplies goods or services.</data>
