    <node id="Consumer">
      <data key="d0">Consumer</data>
      <data key="d1">Stakeholder</data>
      <data key="d2">An entity that purchases or uses goods or services.&lt;SEP&gt;Individuals or entities who use the services or products offered through a system, such as a blockchain.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-522eff26325273b3d80fc7113230a497&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97bf1ff7a9a0ca25ab9f8d5aef1c0355</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Government">
      <data key="d0">Government</data>
      <data key="d1">Organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The **Government** is a multifaceted entity, serving as the governing body of a country, region, nation, state, or community. It is responsible for the system by which a state or community is governed and plays a crucial role in various aspects of citizens' lives. Historically, during the Industrial Revolution, the government was a key organizational unit, managing supply and demand and, consequently, databases. It is often seen as a stakeholder, potentially representing public sector interests in various projects. The government typically supports currencies, although it is noted that Bitcoin is not currently supported by a government. Furthermore, the government is responsible for transferring tasks to councils and is seen as having an important role in the development of blockchain infrastructure and driving long-term social breakthroughs. In this context, it is contrasted with firms and markets.
</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-97bf1ff7a9a0ca25ab9f8d5aef1c0355&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f8fadc0931656aec9e585dab69a412e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30a2cd26d1f20a56ad162067ae77f5e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5438dd33a2364da1b72551b2df52f1d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c03b85bda51716d6730ce96fbafffff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0197eeb8e7c7c337867cce9066008c24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c77900530e329399499bcbd6576bfa88&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d95f9e583e2983dc31135025ee88cc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbba320729446bc75ba3da93887a6890&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79df4317b003b74e86af8cd32e27e5a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ff3172a1b829e75497860c94f161e61&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0158f505b78daad05d6ccc48a0249c4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0dd82da1fab20609f22f1ba5505c2c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0f6ed8dcd79c56128d3004672a382fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d0ad840a38c52ca12523a9fcd7c813a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76a98cc533bce6a2d78638ddd7af06e9</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Citizen">
      <data key="d0">Citizen</data>
      <data key="d1">Stakeholder</data>
      <data key="d2">A member of a community.&lt;SEP&gt;A person who is a legal resident of a country or region.&lt;SEP&gt;An individual who is a member of a city.&lt;SEP&gt;Individuals who are members of a community, often subject to governance by a council.&lt;SEP&gt;Individuals who participate in the participatory society and are affected by government policies.</data>
