    <node id="Protocol">
      <data key="d0">Protocol</data>
      <data key="d1">Protocol</data>
      <data key="d2">A **Protocol** is a comprehensive set of rules and procedures designed to govern various aspects of a system or network. These rules dictate the exchange, transfer, and transmission of data or information between electronic devices, ensuring proper communication and functionality. In the context of blockchain technology, a protocol governs the operation of the blockchain, including verification, governance, and the execution of transactions. It also ensures the secure and controlled circulation of assets, such as bitcoins, by establishing rules for value transfers and preventing double-spending. Protocols can be applied to different blockchain types and are essential for reducing insecurity in transactions, potentially replacing traditional institutions. They often involve processes based on "if-this-then-that" statements, and govern the behavior of a system or network, including communication within a Decentralized Autonomous Organization (DAO).
</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-439e69ca41d62eb2197ac8d9898d5561&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e5c31da27e621b205a1f78e32e74a02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a01d2b4552736dc870cfe78ddc18388&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-522eff26325273b3d80fc7113230a497&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd7c502ce52bde0c777cdbf876a23815&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70d20a99373e00b98325b99305abe639&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae10fd627995a83f8cbe34b2cc884afb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9fc0782a2ca0ad992c87fd04cc684c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0dd82da1fab20609f22f1ba5505c2c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecaf875f9fbc369b9ab166da3e3a5506&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88c1ad4f342b0d4793feb21264904c20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9fb12d3474b8c2ae92a04bb0e1f9c32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35d3d3b65e002a54a8e09b9f90632d33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-efb1e3dfd567d51e6d05f0dc833e60f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce508aba4aa5d17fb6f6c48acdcd7ca8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91caae7bc01e046cb025bd8ce2269321</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Smart Contract">
      <data key="d0">Smart Contract</data>
      <data key="d1">Technology</data>
      <data key="d2">Smart Contracts are self-executing contracts with the terms of the agreement directly written into lines of code. They are stored on a blockchain and are used to automate processes and enforce rules within various ecosystems, including Decentralized Autonomous Organizations (DAOs) and business environments. This technology is a key component for transferring values between seller and buyer and is used to execute transaction workflows. They are essentially programmable rules converted from agreements, often using "If This Then That" statements, and can facilitate processes such as profiling, searching, selecting, approving, contract preparation, ordering, confirming, planning, invoicing, paying, evaluating, registering, administrating, and archiving.
</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ddc340a6853a43e95850d2ba05cf878d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b21a1bc67d35ccf8eb386ac622f736d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70d20a99373e00b98325b99305abe639&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbba320729446bc75ba3da93887a6890&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88c1ad4f342b0d4793feb21264904c20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd7c502ce52bde0c777cdbf876a23815&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3a055a2dc4bcd9be4f15e5ec92c1fe5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4270e4c971112e18b16e21677144a52e</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
