    </node>
    <node id="Trust paradox">
      <data key="d0">Trust paradox</data>
      <data key="d1">Concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The phenomenon where efforts to improve trust can lead to increased distrust.&lt;SEP&gt;The phenomenon where using traditional institutions to reduce trust can increase complexity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7790e270abe48659de241763cc295ace&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e434c5dc41753c53be5ce36200fdf6b</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Transaction">
      <data key="d0">Transaction</data>
      <data key="d1">Concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A **Transaction** is an act of conducting business or other dealings, and is often an exchange or interaction that has taken place, involving the transfer of data or value. It can be an instance of exchanging something of value between two or more parties, or an instance of buying or selling something. Transactions are the core activity that VRM aims to optimize, focusing on reducing costs and complexity.

In the context of a blockchain, a **Transaction** is an action or event recorded on the blockchain, an action or set of actions carried out in the context of a blockchain, and an action that is included in the chain and can no longer leave the chain. It is an action or event that modifies the state of the blockchain, such as the execution of a smart contract or the transfer of value. It is also an exchange of value between a seller and a buyer, recorded on the blockchain, and can include details like date, time, buyer, seller, and product. It can involve money, hours, credits, rights, energy, waste, or other products. It can also refer to the recording of a transaction in a block and from a block in a blockchain. The exchange of something of value, including information, is a key aspect, and the text focuses on the evolution of transactions and the reduction of insecurity.
</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2a295291e4a9f16baa0f819554e218f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0fba0b4043ec1b0d668ebbd78ac72b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68c6d0ac0af7d96b39b1b639efb1632d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddc340a6853a43e95850d2ba05cf878d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b16ddcc5e3e6ea2fab36dc243f642c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9fc0782a2ca0ad992c87fd04cc684c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-760373765c10662d9065ee92ab95d40e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62af45e2578182bc4b36cffed9534e81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-efb1e3dfd567d51e6d05f0dc833e60f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ff2bae129946f137ba1974c04412962&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54ae90ff07e4d84d7a1591868bfd384c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19098cf3a0c49ab4c21a0a5dd8820f48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a18dd982db79e8473ac2f97c0dc81f06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1159f0e0de86630155e1bc94285ff20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-691633ed3dd644b2a539f78fc15edeca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd7c502ce52bde0c777cdbf876a23815&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c3c3f074053a1775cb07219c0c1260d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3a055a2dc4bcd9be4f15e5ec92c1fe5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3616e23745945cf7521047d73b382ad9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9fb12d3474b8c2ae92a04bb0e1f9c32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40c068ec7d9bcc05b8d99949be669665&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b21a1bc67d35ccf8eb386ac622f736d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39148928fd5d1cbfefc9985e1fbb32e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2a72f0d6133d452b3d89271844e2f3b</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Supplier">
      <data key="d0">Supplier</data>
      <data key="d1">Stakeholder</data>
      <data key="d2">A party in a transaction, where trust is needed due to the lack of simultaneous exchange or knowledge of behavior.&lt;SEP&gt;A person or entity that provides goods or services.&lt;SEP&gt;A person who contributes added value within the organization of work.&lt;SEP&gt;An entity that provides goods or services to another entity, incurring marketing costs to be found.&lt;SEP&gt;The entity that can choose an application to profile and offer products and services.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2a295291e4a9f16baa0f819554e218f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddc340a6853a43e95850d2ba05cf878d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f03d2d17c7bf1cc4e87ff716b4c883a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2a72f0d6133d452b3d89271844e2f3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5261cef893d2c990c7504f9ff838aee</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Contract">
      <data key="d0">Contract</data>
      <data key="d1">Concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A formal agreement, either separate or within a company, to achieve a specific objective. Contracts can be with individuals or with a company.&lt;SEP&gt;A tool that can be used to establish trust.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2a295291e4a9f16baa0f819554e218f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2fe75ae1ddcc9a48879a331f1cfc5e4</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Risk of Damage">
      <data key="d0">Risk of Damage</data>
      <data key="d1">Concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A characteristic influencing the organization of trust.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2a295291e4a9f16baa0f819554e218f0</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Delivery Time">
      <data key="d0">Delivery Time</data>
      <data key="d1">Concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A characteristic influencing the organization of trust.&lt;SEP&gt;The time it takes for something to be delivered.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2a295291e4a9f16baa0f819554e218f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b21a1bc67d35ccf8eb386ac622f736d2</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Distance">
      <data key="d0">Distance</data>
      <data key="d1">Concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A characteristic influencing the organization of trust.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2a295291e4a9f16baa0f819554e218f0</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Price">
      <data key="d0">Price</data>
      <data key="d1">Concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A characteristic influencing the organization of trust.&lt;SEP&gt;The amount of money expected or paid for something.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2a295291e4a9f16baa0f819554e218f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b21a1bc67d35ccf8eb386ac622f736d2</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Personal Contact">
      <data key="d0">Personal Contact</data>
      <data key="d1">Concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A characteristic influencing the organization of trust.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2a295291e4a9f16baa0f819554e218f0</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Firm">
      <data key="d0">Firm</data>
      <data key="d1">Organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A **firm** is a business entity, often structured hierarchically, operating within a free market economy. It serves as a key organizational unit, particularly during the Industrial Revolution, responsible for organizing supply and demand and, consequently, databases. The firm can be understood as a business or company, contrasted with the market and government. It is a structure that coordinates internally to reduce insecurity and can be seen as a traditional organizational structure. The firm is often used as an ideal form to organize work, with managers and staff playing a coordinating role.
</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-dcbc07b460eacb096f4663b63a5541e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5438dd33a2364da1b72551b2df52f1d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f8fadc0931656aec9e585dab69a412e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30a2cd26d1f20a56ad162067ae77f5e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd840a5da22869f17616e95321a1be2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1d935bc8938352c154222fd6602c580&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d58bb4eb1c8acda232b201e69b419a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36e21d4687a349e85e73aa7f9938cd18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c205a06d6f77d9602ba2b4ac60c1b9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-efb1e3dfd567d51e6d05f0dc833e60f6</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Market">
      <data key="d0">Market</data>
      <data key="d1">Concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The **Market** is a multifaceted concept, functioning as both a physical and abstract entity. It is fundamentally a system or place where buyers and sellers interact to exchange goods and services. This interaction can occur in various forms, from a regular gathering for the sale of merchandise to a non-transparent system used to organize transactions. The market is an institution that relates to sellers, buyers, and other institutions. It is often contrasted with firms and the government. The market is characterized by flexibility but limited scalability. It also serves as a coordinating capacity between firms, representing the opposite of a firm in terms of scalability and inflexibility. The text also mentions the market as an ideal form, highlighting its role in economic theory and practice, and discusses its relationship with competition and cooperation.
</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f8de7684eaa9214e3bd145ee0ad6dd5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f8fadc0931656aec9e585dab69a412e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-efb1e3dfd567d51e6d05f0dc833e60f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23db6b509ce85251954b0c6eceb7e526&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d58bb4eb1c8acda232b201e69b419a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36e21d4687a349e85e73aa7f9938cd18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fcc88ddd3e1416c5f15ff137621b16b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2982d87bc41ece8bbd334a6d0e1eaf70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c32e29b3b9db8610104f31940dd08f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7a4f0543c997bbae168f719fdd65986</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Blockchain Organizing: foundations for a new social-economic order">
      <data key="d0">Blockchain Organizing: foundations for a new social-economic order</data>
      <data key="d1">Concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A book discussing organizing trust.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2d58bb4eb1c8acda232b201e69b419a6</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ICT system">
      <data key="d0">ICT system</data>
      <data key="d1">System</data>
      <data key="d2">A system that is part of an organization.&lt;SEP&gt;ICT system is a system that uses information and communication technologies. It is mentioned as a tool for coordinating activities.&gt;</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2d58bb4eb1c8acda232b201e69b419a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c205a06d6f77d9602ba2b4ac60c1b9a</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Employees">
      <data key="d0">Employees</data>
      <data key="d1">Stakeholder</data>
      <data key="d2">Employees are individuals who work for an organization and are subject to management and control. They are the recipients of management's efforts in planning, motivating, coordinating, and controlling.&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;Individuals working for the organization.&lt;SEP&gt;Participants in the network community.&lt;SEP&gt;People employed by an organization.&lt;SEP&gt;People who work for an organization.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-439e69ca41d62eb2197ac8d9898d5561&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1d935bc8938352c154222fd6602c580&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d58bb4eb1c8acda232b201e69b419a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c205a06d6f77d9602ba2b4ac60c1b9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba1dbef1dcc5103193b5bebcfc5f3f62</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Organogram">
      <data key="d0">Organogram</data>
      <data key="d1">Component</data>
      <data key="d2">A diagram that shows the structure of an organization.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2d58bb4eb1c8acda232b201e69b419a6</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Structure">
      <data key="d0">Structure</data>
      <data key="d1">Concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The way an organization is set up.&lt;SEP&gt;The way in which something is organized or arranged.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cb325ff3876e609f14b5256360d8deec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d58bb4eb1c8acda232b201e69b419a6</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Culture">
      <data key="d0">Culture</data>
      <data key="d1">Concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The customs, arts, social institutions, and achievements of a particular nation, people, or group.&lt;SEP&gt;The shared values and beliefs of an organization.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e7b4cfcb5217fb678295a92b2dce1add&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8de7684eaa9214e3bd145ee0ad6dd5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d58bb4eb1c8acda232b201e69b419a6</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Scalability">
      <data key="d0">Scalability</data>
      <data key="d1">Concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Scalability refers to the capacity of a system, company, or organization to expand and manage increased workloads or demands effectively. It is considered a significant advantage for a firm, enabling it to grow and broaden its operations. Scalability encompasses the ability of a system or process to handle a growing volume of work in a capable manner, ensuring it can accommodate increasing amounts of work.
</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-01616b5179550e4bd0aa2f4aec943768&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f8fadc0931656aec9e585dab69a412e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69efea1dbe09587f8af78dcc05834412&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d58bb4eb1c8acda232b201e69b419a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2fe75ae1ddcc9a48879a331f1cfc5e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80bcfc5e0491a38a57bdcf5b7453e3c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-158f8bc907835844a3f304c334f72115</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Inflexibility">
      <data key="d0">Inflexibility</data>
      <data key="d1">Concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A disadvantage of a firm.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2d58bb4eb1c8acda232b201e69b419a6</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Bessems &amp; Bril">
      <data key="d0">Bessems &amp; Bril</data>
      <data key="d1">Stakeholder</data>
      <data key="d2">Authors of the book 'Blockchain Organizing: foundations for a new social-economic order'.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2d58bb4eb1c8acda232b201e69b419a6</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Control">
      <data key="d0">Control</data>
      <data key="d1">Concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The act of limiting freedom, often achieved through protocols.&lt;SEP&gt;The act of managing or directing people or things. The leader must dare to let go of control, to give space to self-organizing capacity of project members.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d98a59ed81543294260a33227b3460f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce508aba4aa5d17fb6f6c48acdcd7ca8</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="New Institutional Economics (NIE)">
      <data key="d0">New Institutional Economics (NIE)</data>
      <data key="d1">Concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A field of expertise within economics that deals with tools and the questions that can be solved with these tools. It expands existing economic insights with social and legal standards and rules.&lt;SEP&gt;A theory that explains the need for intermediaries in modern economies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0c32e29b3b9db8610104f31940dd08f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce508aba4aa5d17fb6f6c48acdcd7ca8</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Encryption">
      <data key="d0">Encryption</data>
      <data key="d1">Technology</data>
      <data key="d2">A method of encoding information to secure it.&lt;SEP&gt;The process of converting information into a code to prevent unauthorized access.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ecaf875f9fbc369b9ab166da3e3a5506&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e7516ac1d2c2eabb8e7a0eb0c8233aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce508aba4aa5d17fb6f6c48acdcd7ca8</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Keys">
      <data key="d0">Keys</data>
      <data key="d1">Technology</data>
      <data key="d2">Used in encryption.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ce508aba4aa5d17fb6f6c48acdcd7ca8</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Digital Signature">
      <data key="d0">Digital Signature</data>
      <data key="d1">Technology</data>
      <data key="d2">A cryptographic mechanism used to verify the authenticity of a transaction, created using the private key and verifiable using the public key. It acts as proof of ownership without revealing the private key.&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;A cryptographic technique used to verify the authenticity of a transaction.&lt;SEP&gt;Used in encryption.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-40c068ec7d9bcc05b8d99949be669665&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce508aba4aa5d17fb6f6c48acdcd7ca8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54ae90ff07e4d84d7a1591868bfd384c</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Double Spending">
      <data key="d0">Double Spending</data>
      <data key="d1">Concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A security concern in digital transactions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ce508aba4aa5d17fb6f6c48acdcd7ca8</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Intermediaries">
      <data key="d0">Intermediaries</data>
      <data key="d1">Stakeholder</data>
      <data key="d2">Intermediaries are entities that facilitate transactions or processes between parties, acting between demand and supply. These can be additional entities involved in transactions. Technology, including Blockchain, is reducing or eliminating some of these intermediaries, making some individuals or entities redundant. Smart contracts are one way this is being achieved.
</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d1f2d6d5047300f276afc27cb0492fdb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ff2bae129946f137ba1974c04412962&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4e1aaefe2d119ce580dcd7142980a1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1159f0e0de86630155e1bc94285ff20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6e4f60dfd1366a24d0989693fd1426e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95caf1e3a28dea181e7c30d89b9921b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a9c26deb5facb68529f8f7701c4bd55&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce508aba4aa5d17fb6f6c48acdcd7ca8</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Software">
      <data key="d0">Software</data>
      <data key="d1">Technology</data>
      <data key="d2">Computer programs and related data.&lt;SEP&gt;Generic software, specifically blockchain software in this context.&lt;SEP&gt;Open and free-source software used in the PDS system.&lt;SEP&gt;Software used by nodes to stay compatible with the Bitcoin protocol. Software developers are continuously improving the software but cannot enforce changes in the Bitcoin protocol without convincing others of the use, necessity and efficiency.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a279853919c122eda7df35789ec784fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-544c2611bcdf82d1952de94fef47569e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-439e69ca41d62eb2197ac8d9898d5561&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b0dd8012eae1d2405bd60a07f715200</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Programmers">
      <data key="d0">Programmers</data>
      <data key="d1">Stakeholder</data>
      <data key="d2">Individuals who write and maintain software, particularly blockchain software.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-544c2611bcdf82d1952de94fef47569e</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Designers">
      <data key="d0">Designers</data>
      <data key="d1">Stakeholder</data>
      <data key="d2">Individuals who design systems and interfaces, relevant to blockchain.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-544c2611bcdf82d1952de94fef47569e</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Paradigm Shift">
      <data key="d0">Paradigm Shift</data>
      <data key="d1">Concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A fundamental change in the basic concepts and practices of something.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-544c2611bcdf82d1952de94fef47569e</data>
