    <node id="Company">
      <data key="d0">Company</data>
      <data key="d1">Organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A **Company** is a business entity, formed to conduct business, and is often the central focus of analysis. These entities utilize hierarchical structures to manage employees, cultivate a business culture, and achieve scalability. They operate with a vision, mission, target, and strategy. Companies are characterized by a limited span of control and connection costs, but can be less flexible due to high fixed costs. The text discusses the company as a unit of thinking and its relationship to cooperation and competition, with a focus on its productivity and organizational capacity. In the evolving network economy, companies are shifting their role in solving management problems and organizing trust, potentially becoming major nodes in shared transaction networks. The "old" company can act as a permanent core or hub of a new network organization or "n:n community".
</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fd5472ddb6ce206d59469e54f3662336&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8de7684eaa9214e3bd145ee0ad6dd5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69efea1dbe09587f8af78dcc05834412&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02d52f39ba6d443c4c785ca07baab507&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92a25fd0e21cd743e62c34c35ca67a06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2fe75ae1ddcc9a48879a331f1cfc5e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f15a70031415a373cab08355dc72cc16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bc3db8823c5e5cacf0a55cc60c785f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f77d5a4ad60f6ba2fd71299d648a478&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-efb1e3dfd567d51e6d05f0dc833e60f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7a4f0543c997bbae168f719fdd65986</data>
