    <node id="Process">
      <data key="d0">Process</data>
      <data key="d1">Concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The term "Process" refers to a series of actions or steps taken to achieve a particular end. This concept is relevant in various contexts, including data management, where processes are undergoing changes. Processes are also crucial for the efficient performance of existing organizations. Furthermore, the text mentions the transfer of existing processes to new locations, such as a new building, and the implementation of new rules and procedures within the financial sector, which can be considered as the addition of new processes.
</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-30a2cd26d1f20a56ad162067ae77f5e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd9bd6f99a4d3a44dfd7145bcf2becde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b21a1bc67d35ccf8eb386ac622f736d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bb7630f85643e1cb2d411ec7e989e2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66c04437d924c888b68f0a652726f850&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb325ff3876e609f14b5256360d8deec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e159991e1f1aeb8a0169a48ad5b8333&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-158f8bc907835844a3f304c334f72115</data>
