    </node>
    <node id="Blockchain technology">
      <data key="d0">Blockchain technology</data>
      <data key="d1">Technology</data>
      <data key="d2">Blockchain technology is a distributed, decentralized, public digital ledger that relies on a free and public internet. It is a technology that enables secure and transparent data management and transactions. Blockchain technology can play an important role in finding and connecting people and resources to a project target. It is used to address problems such as fake work, privacy concerns, the power of large tech companies, and fake news. This technology is also used in the context of trust and organizational design. It is the underlying technology upon which applications can be built, and is used by Blockchain Organizing and cryptocurrency. Furthermore, it is the technology that Ethereum applications work with, providing a distributed and immutable ledger.
</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-29858535f8646a6325b1db80639f647f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f9fe9648a4981d3053e59b4400ece92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ef0d0629633d3f8c23f82b65d27b006&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6356289eb89ea3c9fb9f8aeb2f5cfa59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c450f48104718c81f1f7df7492138e83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e434c5dc41753c53be5ce36200fdf6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2a72f0d6133d452b3d89271844e2f3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bdc886b23f3ebaa015732c5dc3db208&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22a4fbd8f76688a6d34610463072b14d</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
