      <data key="d0">Knowledge Centre Blockchain Organizing</data>
      <data key="d1">Organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A resource for up-to-date information on Blockchain Organizing.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6356289eb89ea3c9fb9f8aeb2f5cfa59</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Cryptocurrency">
      <data key="d0">Cryptocurrency</data>
      <data key="d1">Concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A digital or virtual currency that uses cryptography for security.&lt;SEP&gt;A digital or virtual currency that uses cryptography for security. It serves as a medium of exchange.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of digital currency, of which Bitcoin is an example, built on blockchain technology.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fb686b1805befa2a119993ae3948d96b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3be89e365c019f2fcc2432c91f0e473b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6356289eb89ea3c9fb9f8aeb2f5cfa59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae10fd627995a83f8cbe34b2cc884afb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35554d8f41f52c69d22444b00c08876e</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Figure 1.4">
      <data key="d0">Figure 1.4</data>
      <data key="d1">Concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The blockchain iceberg', a visual representation of the relationship between Blockchain Organizing and blockchain technology.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6356289eb89ea3c9fb9f8aeb2f5cfa59</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Decentralized Accounting System">
      <data key="d0">Decentralized Accounting System</data>
      <data key="d1">System</data>
      <data key="d2">A system where transactions are recorded and distributed across participating nodes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ae10fd627995a83f8cbe34b2cc884afb</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Node">
      <data key="d0">Node</data>
      <data key="d1">Component</data>
      <data key="d2">A **Node** is a fundamental component of a network, representing a computer or other device with its own identity connected to the network. Nodes are crucial participants in the Bitcoin and other blockchain networks, playing a vital role in processing transactions and maintaining the network's integrity. They accept incoming connections, receive and transmit data, and facilitate the creation, reception, and transmission of data. Essentially, a Node acts as a single point within a distributed ledger network, contributing to the overall functionality and security of the system.
</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3616e23745945cf7521047d73b382ad9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae10fd627995a83f8cbe34b2cc884afb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f95a0611fe1d32637a403d767d70c8bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91caae7bc01e046cb025bd8ce2269321&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a62990abf7c11921583ee875b388e787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3a055a2dc4bcd9be4f15e5ec92c1fe5</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Cryptography">
      <data key="d0">Cryptography</data>
      <data key="d1">Concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The field of expertise focused on encrypting values and messages using processors to prevent unauthorized access.&lt;SEP&gt;The practice and study of techniques for secure communication in the presence of third parties.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ae10fd627995a83f8cbe34b2cc884afb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c97cbc55e4d5c208212c7c5fab62f82e</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Satoshi Nakamoto">
      <data key="d0">Satoshi Nakamoto</data>
      <data key="d1">Stakeholder</data>
      <data key="d2">The individual who solved the challenge of achieving consensus among generals using the concept of Proof of Work.&lt;SEP&gt;The pseudonym for the creator(s) of Bitcoin, who authored the Bitcoin whitepaper.&lt;SEP&gt;The pseudonymous creator of Bitcoin and the first implementer of blockchain technology.&lt;SEP&gt;The pseudonymous creator of Bitcoin.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ae10fd627995a83f8cbe34b2cc884afb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c97cbc55e4d5c208212c7c5fab62f82e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b16ddcc5e3e6ea2fab36dc243f642c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22a4fbd8f76688a6d34610463072b14d</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Ethereum">
      <data key="d0">Ethereum</data>
      <data key="d1">Technology</data>
      <data key="d2">Ethereum is a blockchain platform, initially conceived in 2013 by a group of programmers led by Vitalik Buterin as an extension of the Bitcoin protocol. It is a decentralized, permissionless platform managed by the Ethereum Foundation, designed to facilitate a broader range of values beyond just currency. Ethereum serves as an operating system and enables the development of decentralized applications (dApps) and smart contracts. It has grown into a platform for developing applications that work with blockchain technology. Ethereum is also a cryptocurrency, mentioned in relation to Bitcoin and its response to security breaches.
</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4d9c783fe7141c81f49edd0fdc5f7e7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c7ba153eb5a0d7f103744153505eb9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5655831cfa4533792e479b8fbd6fa983&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c450f48104718c81f1f7df7492138e83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae10fd627995a83f8cbe34b2cc884afb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f95a0611fe1d32637a403d767d70c8bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62af45e2578182bc4b36cffed9534e81</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="The DAO">
      <data key="d0">The DAO</data>
      <data key="d1">Organization</data>
      <data key="d2">An organization related to Ethereum that experienced a security breach and subsequently underwent a hard fork.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ae10fd627995a83f8cbe34b2cc884afb</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Hard-fork">
      <data key="d0">Hard-fork</data>
      <data key="d1">Process</data>
      <data key="d2">A split in the blockchain, allowing for changes to the history of the chain, as chosen by The DAO.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ae10fd627995a83f8cbe34b2cc884afb</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Miner">
      <data key="d0">Miner</data>
      <data key="d1">Stakeholder</data>
      <data key="d2">A participant in the Bitcoin network who adds blocks to the blockchain by solving a puzzle and receives bitcoins as a reward.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ae10fd627995a83f8cbe34b2cc884afb</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Block">
      <data key="d0">Block</data>
      <data key="d1">Component</data>
      <data key="d2">A collection of transactions added to the blockchain.&lt;SEP&gt;A collection of transactions in the blockchain.&lt;SEP&gt;A collection of transactions recorded on the blockchain.&lt;SEP&gt;A collection of transactions that have taken place at the same time. It is added to the blockchain and includes a previous and next block.&lt;SEP&gt;A unit of data added to the blockchain by a miner.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-69b08a16c5fa8b5090e0317a4cf1d8ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3616e23745945cf7521047d73b382ad9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19098cf3a0c49ab4c21a0a5dd8820f48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae10fd627995a83f8cbe34b2cc884afb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40c068ec7d9bcc05b8d99949be669665</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Distributed Ledger Technology (DLT)">
      <data key="d0">Distributed Ledger Technology (DLT)</data>
      <data key="d1">Technology</data>
      <data key="d2">A technology to maintain a distributed administration system. It is part of a wider field.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3616e23745945cf7521047d73b382ad9</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="User">
      <data key="d0">User</data>
      <data key="d1">Stakeholder</data>
      <data key="d2">A person who checks the transactions on the chain.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3616e23745945cf7521047d73b382ad9</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Administration System">
      <data key="d0">Administration System</data>
      <data key="d1">System</data>
      <data key="d2">A system that tracks value, deductions when sending, and additions when receiving.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f9fc0782a2ca0ad992c87fd04cc684c1</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Value">
      <data key="d0">Value</data>
      <data key="d1">Concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Value is a fundamental concept in Blockchain Organizing, representing something that has worth or importance. It can be a concept related to Blockchain Organizing, a resource, or something that has monetary worth. Value is assigned by a person and is recognizable and distinguishable from other values through its attributes. It can also refer to the worth of products, services, Bitcoin, and other currencies. The amount or quantity of something, especially in the context of a transaction, also represents value. Shared values within a community are considered the most important connection in Blockchain Organizing.
</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1900d9fbbbeb4ce6f5731ed0181e0729&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e7516ac1d2c2eabb8e7a0eb0c8233aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3601da3b0bece1d5e1adfbd71567fa8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19098cf3a0c49ab4c21a0a5dd8820f48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0158f505b78daad05d6ccc48a0249c4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9fc0782a2ca0ad992c87fd04cc684c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0dd82da1fab20609f22f1ba5505c2c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-691633ed3dd644b2a539f78fc15edeca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c3d3368ceab3c771201196039066576&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-248aad6ba79eb8e5e5f575bda42587cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0697bcc736e38c4eecf7ba0b89208980</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Transaction Costs">
      <data key="d0">Transaction Costs</data>
      <data key="d1">Concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Transaction Costs refer to the various expenses involved in carrying out an economic exchange or transaction. These costs encompass a range of activities, including finding a supplier, creating contracts, managing payments and security, and the overall process of outsourcing work. They include marketing costs, contract costs, payment and security costs, search costs, information costs, bargaining costs, and enforcement costs. Organizational technology, such as blockchain, aims to minimize these costs.
</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2e4d7c93b13ce48f7dc9be0964a62044&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ff2bae129946f137ba1974c04412962&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7a4f0543c997bbae168f719fdd65986&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92a25fd0e21cd743e62c34c35ca67a06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b21a1bc67d35ccf8eb386ac622f736d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fd9ad798afc21b7973e26b6f138852e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33012de7a0074f352d461a49b8eb5bc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5261cef893d2c990c7504f9ff838aee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f0573de7c7cbde2e2975eead953b1b1</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Entrepreneurs">
      <data key="d0">Entrepreneurs</data>
      <data key="d1">Stakeholder</data>
      <data key="d2">Entities that are stakeholders in the project.&lt;SEP&gt;Individuals who start and run their own businesses, often with innovative ideas. They are supported by the Foundation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d5f5768652d04cf68f3ca04301ae0b84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f0573de7c7cbde2e2975eead953b1b1</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Intrapreneurs">
      <data key="d0">Intrapreneurs</data>
      <data key="d1">Stakeholder</data>
      <data key="d2">Individuals who work within an existing organization to develop new products or services. They are supported by the Foundation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8f0573de7c7cbde2e2975eead953b1b1</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Digital Values">
      <data key="d0">Digital Values</data>
      <data key="d1">Concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Digital products and services, such as e-books or paid newspaper articles, and information about products and services.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8f0573de7c7cbde2e2975eead953b1b1</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Demand and Supply">
      <data key="d0">Demand and Supply</data>
      <data key="d1">Concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The economic forces that interact to determine the price and quantity of goods and services. Blockchain Organizing aims to organize these efficiently.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8f0573de7c7cbde2e2975eead953b1b1</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TCP/IP">
      <data key="d0">TCP/IP</data>
      <data key="d1">Protocol</data>
      <data key="d2">A communication protocol designed by Vint Cerf and Robert Kahn, used for internet communication.&lt;SEP&gt;A communication protocol used for exchanging data over a network.&lt;SEP&gt;A standard protocol used for communication over the internet.&lt;SEP&gt;A suite of communication protocols used for the internet. The text mentions that early communication applications worked with the TCP/IP protocol.&lt;SEP&gt;A suite of communication protocols used on the Internet and other computer networks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2ff2bae129946f137ba1974c04412962&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d8c581b75ce0f3a97084b5afbc810e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0fba0b4043ec1b0d668ebbd78ac72b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4322631c6ab79cfbe8d80ecc2f1dee23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22a4fbd8f76688a6d34610463072b14d</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Nodes">
      <data key="d0">Nodes</data>
      <data key="d1">Component</data>
      <data key="d2">Nodes are components within a distributed ledger network, specifically individual computers or devices, that participate in a blockchain network. These network components, which can number in the thousands, are responsible for verifying and validating transactions, as well as storing the blockchain. They also forward transactions within the network. To remain compatible, nodes must utilize software that can cooperate with the underlying system stack.
</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6b0dd8012eae1d2405bd60a07f715200&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d666492c06b72b3acdaaf417a46ebbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d8c581b75ce0f3a97084b5afbc810e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0fba0b4043ec1b0d668ebbd78ac72b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-522eff26325273b3d80fc7113230a497&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04f3d062a707dfb7235caa4e344995d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e26104e999e886225d6dd670f42acb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40c068ec7d9bcc05b8d99949be669665</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Bitcoin protocol">
      <data key="d0">Bitcoin protocol</data>
      <data key="d1">Protocol</data>
      <data key="d2">The Bitcoin protocol is a protocol that underpins the Bitcoin cryptocurrency, designed for secure and decentralized transactions. It governs the operation of Bitcoin, including wallet software downloading, mining, key creation, hash function implementation, transaction management, and block inclusion. This protocol enables the Bitcoin network and is similar to the protocol that makes e-mail traffic possible. It is controlled, updated, and managed by a community of users and developers, requiring a degree of agreement among users to function. The protocol relies on distributed computing power and is used to prevent fraud within the Bitcoin system. Ethereum is an extension of this protocol.
</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6b0dd8012eae1d2405bd60a07f715200&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69b08a16c5fa8b5090e0317a4cf1d8ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d8c581b75ce0f3a97084b5afbc810e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19098cf3a0c49ab4c21a0a5dd8820f48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c450f48104718c81f1f7df7492138e83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b16ddcc5e3e6ea2fab36dc243f642c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f95a0611fe1d32637a403d767d70c8bb</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Wallet software">
      <data key="d0">Wallet software</data>
      <data key="d1">Component</data>
      <data key="d2">Software used for managing Bitcoin wallets, including downloading functionality.&lt;SEP&gt;Software within a Bitcoin node that manages digital currency.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4d8c581b75ce0f3a97084b5afbc810e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69b08a16c5fa8b5090e0317a4cf1d8ca</data>
