    <node id="Seller">
      <data key="d0">Seller</data>
      <data key="d1">Stakeholder</data>
      <data key="d2">The **Seller** is a party involved in a transaction, specifically the one offering goods or services for sale. This entity possesses value and transfers it to another party. The seller can be an individual or another entity, and they are responsible for selling a product or service. In the context of a VRM (Vendor Relationship Management) model, the seller is the entity that is not in control. The seller must also be able to prove ownership of the value being transferred.
</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2ebde21af6f93489c1d70ecb9ced229b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0c88e24a0ff0bacee61712e00986bcd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e7516ac1d2c2eabb8e7a0eb0c8233aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a18dd982db79e8473ac2f97c0dc81f06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b21a1bc67d35ccf8eb386ac622f736d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66c04437d924c888b68f0a652726f850&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fcc88ddd3e1416c5f15ff137621b16b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-691633ed3dd644b2a539f78fc15edeca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9fb12d3474b8c2ae92a04bb0e1f9c32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee92635ddcf90a64b087c72dedf9473d</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Governance Model">
      <data key="d0">Governance Model</data>
      <data key="d1">Concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A system for managing and making decisions within the community.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2e7516ac1d2c2eabb8e7a0eb0c8233aa</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Open Source">
      <data key="d0">Open Source</data>
      <data key="d1">Concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A development model where the source code is publicly available and can be modified by anyone.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2e7516ac1d2c2eabb8e7a0eb0c8233aa</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Tokens">
      <data key="d0">Tokens</data>
      <data key="d1">Concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Digital assets that can be used within the Blockchain ecosystem.&lt;SEP&gt;Units received for contributing to a community, exchangeable for services or other resources.&lt;SEP&gt;Units used for transactions, representing value. Examples include hours, credits, rights, energy, waste, products, or services.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f90a9e3d42822d671bf599944b3ba7ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e7516ac1d2c2eabb8e7a0eb0c8233aa</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Bitcoins">
      <data key="d0">Bitcoins</data>
      <data key="d1">Technology</data>
      <data key="d2">A specific type of cryptocurrency.&lt;SEP&gt;Cryptographic digital money, a form of currency. Its value is derived from trust and belief.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b0dd82da1fab20609f22f1ba5505c2c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e7516ac1d2c2eabb8e7a0eb0c8233aa</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Miners">
      <data key="d0">Miners</data>
      <data key="d1">Stakeholder</data>
      <data key="d2">Miners are entities involved in the validation and addition of new blocks to a blockchain, particularly in permissionless systems. They play a crucial role in providing security and control over input references and preventing double-spending. These individuals or entities validate transactions on the blockchain, contributing to the verification process within the network. In the context of Bitcoin, miners often solve mathematical puzzles as part of their transaction verification duties. Essentially, miners are participants in the blockchain network who verify transactions.
</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-01616b5179550e4bd0aa2f4aec943768&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-522eff26325273b3d80fc7113230a497&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e7516ac1d2c2eabb8e7a0eb0c8233aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f90a9e3d42822d671bf599944b3ba7ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f95a0611fe1d32637a403d767d70c8bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40c068ec7d9bcc05b8d99949be669665</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Third Parties">
      <data key="d0">Third Parties</data>
      <data key="d1">Stakeholder</data>
      <data key="d2">Trusted entities that can reduce insecurity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2e7516ac1d2c2eabb8e7a0eb0c8233aa</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Supply Chain">
      <data key="d0">Supply Chain</data>
      <data key="d1">Concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A chain of actors, from source to consumption.&lt;SEP&gt;A network of intermediaries between the first seller and final buyer, typically involving 1:1 or 1:n relationships.&lt;SEP&gt;A network of organizations, people, activities, information, and resources involved in moving a product or service from supplier to customer.&lt;SEP&gt;A system focused on the flow of goods and services, aiming to improve productivity.&lt;SEP&gt;A system of organizations, people, activities, information, and resources involved in moving a product or service from supplier to customer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-439e69ca41d62eb2197ac8d9898d5561&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f03d2d17c7bf1cc4e87ff716b4c883a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a9c26deb5facb68529f8f7701c4bd55&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd10a20a830bf4ba4fd072ae7212cb97&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4270e4c971112e18b16e21677144a52e</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
