    <node id="Cooperation">
      <data key="d0">Cooperation</data>
      <data key="d1">Concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Cooperation is a collaborative relationship between organizations and various entities. It is a concept presented as having a higher chance of survival than competition in a social context. Cooperation involves working together to achieve a common goal, such as organizing the supply and demand of data or developing technical innovations. This act of working together, often within or between organizations, is a key aspect of organizing and a counterpart to competing. It is frequently cited as a desired state but can be challenging to implement effectively.
</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0f8fadc0931656aec9e585dab69a412e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23db6b509ce85251954b0c6eceb7e526&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b33ea2da57d21a7eb6228fb95e11f197&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bc3db8823c5e5cacf0a55cc60c785f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5ddf3937d82ce7155cb82041f93c070&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b863d6e3078036af759c206058182dc</data>
