    <node id="Supply and Demand">
      <data key="d0">Supply and Demand</data>
      <data key="d1">Concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Supply and Demand is a core economic concept and an economic model that describes the relationship between the availability of a product or service and the desire for it. These economic forces determine prices and influence the price and quantity of goods and services. They drive the production, distribution, and consumption of goods and services. The balance of Supply and Demand is affected by coordinating mechanisms. VRM seeks to organize these economic forces, which are the amount of a product or service available and the desire of buyers for it, considered as factors regulating its price. It is the relationship between the amount of a commodity that producers are willing to sell at various prices and the amount that consumers are willing to buy.
</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d416cde8eabae677d0912ce737cda600&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a18dd982db79e8473ac2f97c0dc81f06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fd9ad798afc21b7973e26b6f138852e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1159f0e0de86630155e1bc94285ff20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b33ea2da57d21a7eb6228fb95e11f197&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cdfa9a12c73aebf9f439468bb7d05f82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4dff72475ff38066f492d4c69fb7ef24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40c068ec7d9bcc05b8d99949be669665&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a077a85d3f0dd5b451d9b582ad0180e</data>
