    <node id="Database">
      <data key="d0">Database</data>
      <data key="d1">Concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A **Database** is a structured collection of data, serving as a storage tool for attributes and their values, similar to a warehouse. It is designed for efficient storage and retrieval and can be held in a computer, making it accessible in various ways. The term's origins and function are discussed in the context of its evolution, including its relationship to societal changes. A database can also be a data structure, model, or description, and is a crucial component of blockchain infrastructure. In the context of Bitcoin, it refers to the complete database of transactions. Traditionally, databases were physical archives for recording, storing, consulting, and deleting digital data. Furthermore, it is a system for storing and managing data, with blockchain databases being a specific type.
</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2d666492c06b72b3acdaaf417a46ebbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ff2bae129946f137ba1974c04412962&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30a2cd26d1f20a56ad162067ae77f5e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77b4bcb1ad6558b972215f2dcea8a2ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d005bac0574e1b7fd4947857f5f5518c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-958ad09cd25418d23c3d7174c3c1a2f7</data>
