    <node id="PDS">
      <data key="d0">PDS</data>
      <data key="d1">Concept</data>
      <data key="d2">PDS, which stands for Personal Data Services, Personal Data Store, and Personal Data Systems, is a system designed to give individuals greater control over their personal data. It is a core component of systems like Blockchain Organizing and VRM (Vendor Relationship Management) and is particularly relevant in light of stricter privacy regulations like GDPR. The primary goal of PDS is to empower individuals to manage their data, including controlling access and storage. This is achieved through a decentralized system where users (sellers) can maintain their profiles and grant permissions for data use. Data is stored in a decentralized manner, with a unique key used to retrieve additional attributes from an off-chain location.
</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c4f81d4cc8144b69f5b3cc66ebd2a9ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c514e71a44aea9915f71ae5b109dc21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0c88e24a0ff0bacee61712e00986bcd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1d935bc8938352c154222fd6602c580&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a279853919c122eda7df35789ec784fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61f13cb789bea7683db5372a497cf9b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3a055a2dc4bcd9be4f15e5ec92c1fe5</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
