    <node id="DAO">
      <data key="d0">DAO</data>
      <data key="d1">Organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A decentralized autonomous organization (DAO) is an organization represented by rules encoded as a computer program that is transparent, controlled by the organization members and not influenced by a central government. DAOs are characterized by their use of smart contracts, which automate processes and enforce rules. DAOs are often used to manage digital assets, make decisions, and coordinate activities. They are designed to be transparent and secure, with all transactions and decisions recorded on a blockchain."&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;Decentralized Autonomous Organizations, programmable institutions using blockchain technology.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6f6e57e76e58e2792cffba385c065f41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88c1ad4f342b0d4793feb21264904c20</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="IFTTT statement">
      <data key="d0">IFTTT statement</data>
      <data key="d1">Concept</data>
      <data key="d2">An 'If This Then That' statement, a simple conditional statement used in programming and automation. In this context, it refers to the basic building blocks of smart contracts."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-88c1ad4f342b0d4793feb21264904c20</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
