    </node>
    <node id="Immanuel Kant">
      <data key="d0">Immanuel Kant</data>
      <data key="d1">Stakeholder</data>
      <data key="d2">One of the best-known Enlighteners, whose offers the following insight: “Enlightenment is man’s emergence from his self-imposed immaturity. Immaturity is the inability to use one’s understanding without guidance from another. 194”</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2a92881103af33d8dccba6a7ad854108</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Concept">
      <data key="d0">Concept</data>
      <data key="d1">Enlightenment</data>
      <data key="d2">The **Concept** refers to a state of being characterized by a refusal to be led by others. It encompasses ideas like shifting blame onto others, as opposed to taking responsibility for one's own actions. This concept is often associated with a self-imposed immaturity, which is defined as the inability to utilize one's own understanding without relying on external guidance. This concept is often used by people and is frequently compared to them.
</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2a92881103af33d8dccba6a7ad854108</data>
      <data key="d4">WB8_BlockchainOrganizing_Managers_book8p1v1_UK_KOPIE_INTERN_GERBRUIK (1).txt</data>
    </node>
